;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-16, for Phase 17 step 5
;; (doc/developer/vms-sdl-interfaces.md, part 12, proposal 1, approved by
;; the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-16. It replaces the file the
;; user reviewed earlier that day. Why this is right:
;; - LockStatusBlock, new, is $ENQ's lock status block: its type
;;   descriptor (.LONG 24) is like IOStatusBlock's, with no pointers to
;;   trace. Its fields are each aligned to their size, which is VMS's
;;   layout: status 0, reserved 2, lockId 4, value 8 to 23.
;; - The header comment names it (one line more) and its declaration with
;;   its comment is 12 lines, so every line number after it, and each
;;   trap's PUSHL of one, is 13 more; the module's key (.IDENT, POC_K1_)
;;   is new, as its interface changed. No code changes.
;; As the user reviewed it on 2026-10-16 (part 7, proposal 2):
;; - ArrayDescriptor, new, is a CLASS_A descriptor's prototype block, 16
;;   bytes: its type descriptor (.LONG 16) is like StringDescriptor's,
;;   with no pointers to trace. Its fields are each aligned to their size,
;;   which is VMS's layout: length 0, type 2, class 3, address 4, scale 8,
;;   digits 9, flags 10, dimensions 11, size 12.
;; - DescribeArray, new, stores LEN(elements, 1), the element's length,
;;   through Card16 (its CALLG with the length from 20(AP)), 14 and 4 as
;;   bytes, the array's address, 0 into the scale, digits and flags
;;   (CLRB), 1 dimension, and LEN(elements) * LEN(elements, 1) (16(AP) and
;;   20(AP), the dope vector after the array's address at 12(AP); the
;;   descriptor's tag is at 8(AP)) into the size. SYSTEM.VAL to CARD32 of
;;   a LONGINT is a MOVL.
;; - The header comment is three lines longer, classA one and
;;   ArrayDescriptor 15, so every line number after them, and each trap's
;;   PUSHL of one, is 19 more until DescribeArray, then 33 more; the
;;   module's key (.IDENT, POC_K1_) is new, as its interface changed.
;; As the user reviewed it on 2026-10-15:
;; - The lengths, counts, a descriptor's class and data type, and an I/O
;;   status are CARDs now; each has its signed twin's size, so no layout
;;   changes, and the module's key (.IDENT, POC_K1_) is new.
;; - Card16, new, gives SetItem's buffer length and Describe's length as
;;   a CARD16: SYSTEM.VAL(SYSTEM.CARD16, n) is n's low word, MOVZWL
;;   -4(FP), R0 from n's copy in the frame, zero-extended as a CARD's
;;   result is; a function that reached its END would trap (12, line
;;   80). SetItem's and Describe's CALLG go to it in place of Word's;
;;   Word stays for the item code, which may be negative.
;; - The header comment is three lines longer, so every line number
;;   after it, and each trap's PUSHL of one, is 3 more, then 9 more
;;   after Card16.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-14:
;; - VmsArguments has no code of its own beyond its three procedures and
;;   Word: its types' layouts are poc's ordinary ones, each field aligned
;;   to its size, which are VMS's (StringDescriptor 8 bytes, length at 0,
;;   class and type at 2 and 3, address at 4; ItemListEntry3 12 bytes;
;;   ItemListEntry2 and IOStatusBlock 8).
;; - Word turns a length or code of 0 to 65,535 into the word VMS reads:
;;   over 32,767 it subtracts 65,536 (SUBL2), and the word is the
;;   value's low one, SYSTEM.VAL's truncation (CVTWL -4(FP), R0).
;; - Describe counts up to the first 0X, LEN or 65,535, and stores the
;;   length (Word's), 14 and 1 as bytes, and the text's address; its
;;   descriptor is a VAR record parameter of an Oberon procedure, so its
;;   tag is at 8(AP) and text at 12(AP), with its length at 16(AP).
;; - SetItem stores LEN(buffer), the byte size of an ARRAY OF SYSTEM.BYTE
;;   (24(AP)), cut to 65,535, the code, and the two addresses, each
;;   element of list checked against its length (trap 2); EndList clears
;;   the entry.
